# Developer documentation (`doc/`)

Index: `doc/index.rst`. Do not invent a parallel layout; follow these files.

**Always** read `doc/architecture.rst` before changing layers, threads,
blackboards, device drivers, network/HTTP, or where a type belongs.

For UI colour, map overlays, dialogs, touch/hold, screen rectangles,
scrolling, and in-flight / cockpit safety, read **User interface
guidelines** in `doc/architecture.rst` (including **Cockpit
principles**). Which rectangle an element belongs in is **Screen
rectangles** in that file. External HF anchors (NASA colour, FAA EFB
DOT/FAA/AR-03/67, ICAO Annex 4) are listed there.

Do not invent a parallel colour or gesture language. Reuse named
colours in Look code; keep high saturation and contrast for warnings
and cautions.

User-facing behaviour also needs the **English user manual**
(`doc/manual/en/`), not only `NEWS.txt`. See `.cursor/rules/user-manual.mdc`.

